# Repo-root build context for both Dockerfiles (apps/web, services/api — see
# infra/docker-compose.yml `context: ..`). Keeps secrets
# and host junk OUT of every image layer: without this, `COPY . .` bakes the
# populated root .env (JWT/S3/TURN secrets), .git history and
# host-platform node_modules into builder AND runtime stages.
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.expo
# Both forms: a .dockerignore pattern is matched against the path relative to
# the context root and `*` does not cross `/`, so a bare `coverage` misses
# packages/sync-core/coverage — which `pnpm test` really does produce (the
# sync-core suite runs vitest --coverage) and `COPY . .` really would bake in.
coverage
**/coverage
.env
.env.*
# Local Atlas secrets file — not matched by `.env.*` (no leading dot in the
# stem), and a CLI-context build (`railway up`, `docker build`) would bake it.
atlas-credentials.env
*credentials*.env
# Host junk and build residue. All are gitignored, so they only ever reach a
# build context from a working tree — which is exactly what a CLI-context
# build sends.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
